      "step_number": 1,
      "text": "Step 1: The original parabola has the equation \\( y = ax^2 + bx + c \\) with vertex \\((h, k)\\). The vertex form of a parabola is \\( y = a(x - h)^2 + k \\).",
      "z": -2.347076710659045
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 315,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 317,
      "char_start": 155,
      "effective_step": 2,
      "end_token_index": 106,
      "feature_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "near_end": false,
      "prefix_token_count": 107,
      "q": 0.055417284326313085,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 2,
      "text": "Step 2: Reflecting the parabola about the line \\( y = k \\) means that for every point \\((x, y)\\) on the original parabola, its reflection will be \\((x, 2k - y)\\).",
      "z": -2.8358517227132887
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 573,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 574,
      "char_start": 319,
      "effective_step": 3,
      "end_token_index": 200,
      "feature_source": "stage2_saved_hidden_states[19]",
      "near_end": false,
      "prefix_token_count": 201,
      "q": 0.21853365282731757,
      "q_source": "stage2_test_predictions.csv",
      "step_number": 3,
      "text": "Step 3: To find the equation of the reflected parabola, we substitute \\( y = 2k - (a(x - h)^2 + k) \\) into the reflected equation. Simplifying this gives:\n\\[ y = 2k - a(x - h)^2 - k = k - a(x - h)^2. \\]\nThis can be rewritten as:\n\\[ y = -a(x - h)^2 + k. \\]",
      "z": -1.2742320669026732
    },
    {
      "aligned_char_end": 817,
      "boundary_aligned_back": true,
      "char_end": 819,
      "char_start": 576,
      "effective_step": 4,
